{"cwe": "CWE-329", "severity": "WARNING", "verdict": "Confirm", "explanation": "CBC mode uses a constant EMPTY IV for every message: identical prefixes encrypt identically and an empty IV is trivially predictable. Use a fresh random IV per encryption (or GCM). Real finding -> Confirm.", "patch": "from Crypto.Cipher import AES
def enc(key, data):
    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_GCM)
    ct, tag = cipher.encrypt_and_digest(data)
    return cipher.nonce + tag + ct"}

{"cwe": "CWE-321", "severity": "WARNING", "verdict": "Confirm", "explanation": "A real AES key is hard-coded inline in source. Any key committed to code is compromised and cannot be rotated without redeploys. Real finding -> Confirm.", "patch": "from Crypto.Cipher import AES
def seal(payload):
